{
  "name": "SettingClassIsAType",
  "comment": "A type is named by its namespace, read from the root it lives under (ruling 7, decision\n752). A module's type drops `app.module.` and its `type.` folder; the llm settings class\nlives at app.module.llm.setting, so its name is `llm.setting` — a type of its own, not a\nkind under a shared `setting` family (the family of decision 48 existed only to dodge the\nclash). Looking the type up by its namespace name answers with that name.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "set %t% = %!app.type[\"llm.setting\"]%",
